body:
@justinian Yes, I have also managed to trigger it without GPUParticles3D sometimes. The 3D model importer tooltips trigger it very often, and sometimes but very rarely even without either of those. It is literally just the fact that you are sending NVidia server the order to create an additional window from an additional window, and something scuffs the entire process on Nvidia side.

I had to switch on "single window mode" from Godot settings which stops the freezes. But it is limiting Godot functionality such as embedding and multi-display setups, which is annoying sacrifice just to circumvent the bug. I still recommend giving it a try because anything is better than the freezes that send your entire desktop into recovery.

I'm also considering on forking custom version of Godot with tooltips disabled, it's a single line change in the entire codebase. Perfect fix would be an option to always render tooltips in existing windows rather than pedantically creating new operating system level windows for those little boxes.

> I recall we tried to favor Mailbox V-Sync at some point, but there were issues on NVIDIA + X11 specifically.

Thank you for your thoughts, I really appreciate the comment and references.
In [my proposed patch](https://gist.github.com/bearlikelion/9519e4aaa5807b84e6ca028819025ad9) this is highly targeted to be platform specific _only_ making this change to Wayland Compositors on NVIDIA, I'm not sure the best route to take with fixing this issue and would like some more input and feedback before submitting a proper PR vs `master` 

```
+	if (present_mode == VK_PRESENT_MODE_FIFO_KHR &&
+			physical_device_properties.vendorID == RenderingContextDriver::Vendor::VENDOR_NVIDIA &&
+			GLOBAL_GET("rendering/rendering_device/vulkan/nvidia_prefer_mailbox_present")) {
+		if (present_modes.has(VK_PRESENT_MODE_MAILBOX_KHR)) {
+			present_mode = VK_PRESENT_MODE_MAILBOX_KHR;
+			present_mode_name = "Mailbox (NVIDIA Wayland workaround)";
+		}
+	}
```

@deralmas  your thoughts would be greatly appreciated
